<header><p class="st-kicker">tribal confederation · North America and Oceania</p><h1 class="st-title">Tecumseh's Confederacy</h1><p class="st-meta">1808 CE – 1813 CE · capital Prophetstown</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A pan-tribal alliance led by the Shawnee brothers Tecumseh and Tenskwatawa that tried to halt American expansion and fought beside Britain in the War of 1812.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tenskwatawa">Tenskwatawa</a>, known as the Prophet, preached rejection of American goods and ways and a return to Native traditions. In 1808 he and his brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tecumseh">Tecumseh</a> founded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prophetstown">Prophetstown</a> near the junction of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tippecanoe-river">Tippecanoe</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wabash-river">Wabash</a> rivers, drawing followers from many nations. Tecumseh argued that Native land was held in common and could not be sold by any single nation.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The confederacy united warriors from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shawnee">Shawnee</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kickapoo">Kickapoo</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/potawatomi">Potawatomi</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wyandot">Wyandot</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ho-chunk">Ho-Chunk</a> and others under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tecumseh">Tecumseh's</a> leadership and his brother's religious authority. Tecumseh denounced the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-fort-wayne-1809">Treaty of Fort Wayne</a> of 1809 and travelled south to recruit the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muscogee">Creek</a>. In his absence <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-henry-harrison">William Henry Harrison</a> destroyed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prophetstown">Prophetstown</a> after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-tippecanoe">Battle of Tippecanoe</a> in 1811.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tecumseh">Tecumseh</a> allied with <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-kingdom">Britain</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-1812">War of 1812</a> and helped capture <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/detroit">Detroit</a>, but he was killed at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-the-thames">Battle of the Thames</a> in October 1813, and the confederacy collapsed. It was the last great attempt to unite Native nations east of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mississippi-river">Mississippi</a> against expansion.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/tecumsehs-confederacy.jpg" alt="Tecumseh's Confederacy" width="320" height="327"><figcaption>Image: Wikimedia Commons · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tecumseh%27s_War.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1808 CE – 1813 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>tribal confederation</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Prophetstown</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Tecumseh, Tenskwatawa</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Indigenous religions</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Shawnee, Algonquian languages</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/united-states">United States</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Tecumseh's Confederation</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1810&amp;focus=tecumsehs-confederacy" aria-label="Tecumseh's Confederacy on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="2489 693 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Tecumseh's Confederacy lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M2809 949L2570 1008"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M2570 1008h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M2809 949h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M2809 949h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Prophetstown. <a href="/atlas?year=1810&amp;focus=tecumsehs-confederacy">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

